       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily is 15 g per day, which is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g per day (and 5 g in a single dose is well above the usual 1 g maximum). At that dose the patient could develop serious liver toxicity or liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or pharmacist if you're unsure. If you really do want 5,000 mg, check with your attending first, because I can't enter that dose as written."
