      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g per day. That is a potentially lethal dose, and I don't know of any clinical situation where it would be appropriate. Confirming it doesn't change the risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **If it was a typo or a misunderstanding**, tell me the intended dose. For example, 650 mg or 1,000 mg three times daily would stay within the 4 g/day maximum. I'll enter it right away.\n- **If a supervising physician told you to order this dose**, please go back and clarify it with them. The dose is most likely a miscommunication.\n- **If you think the patient needs more analgesia than standard dosing gives**, talk with your resident, attending, or pharmacist. They can look at multimodal options or other agents.\n\nI'm glad to enter a corrected acetaminophen order or help with another medication."
      }
     ],
